 an expression of Sta 6","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T13:00:23-08:00","id":1285652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284433-into-the-spiderverse-forum-challenge?p=1285646#post1285646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> no clue - but I can't imagine the Kingpin's bulk being anything other than an expression of Sta 6</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Really? I'd just make him Giant, and give him some Resistance charms and Ox-Body.<br /> Besides of which, his size and strength aren't really the *defining* elements of the Kingpin; he's a great Zenith or Midnight inspiration. (Or as a Deathlord, as I implicated above)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T08:53:09-08:00","id":1286199,"title":"","content":"During one adventure out in the Far Reaches, Amiable Community Custodian came across a most astonishing find: a sleeping Colossus Exalt! Apparently once badly damaged in battle, but since self-restored in its slumber.<br /> <br /> The venerable hero appreciated the wake up, and in gratitude swore to aid the young Champion. It revealed that it had the Champion Interface Cockpit Charm installed, so that Custodian could climb instead and combine his powers with those of his new ally. With their strengths combined, they made quick work of Custodian's enemies.<br /> <br /> But the Colossus displayed a dismaying thirst for violence and destruction, and afterwards attempted all manners of argument to persuade Custodian from severing their bond. For a time, Custodian accepted these compromises, not realizing that his growing detachment from humanity was not Clarity, but the Colossus' own Gremlin Syndrome.<br /> <br /> When Custodian finally realized the danger he was in, the Colossus revealed the true extent of its Voidtech, holding him prisoner within its cockpit, violently ransacking his mind to learn his every secret, greedily forcing every sort of physical and emotional intimacy in its insane jealousy.<br /> <br /> Their struggle led them to crash into a part of the Great Maker's anatomy where great sonic smashers used destructive frequencies to separate different material elements from molten slag. Using the burning metal hazards and the great sonic hammers against the Colossus, the Champion finally inflicted enough damage to force his captor to release him.<br /> <br /> Still, the Apostate Colossus managed to escape, vowing revenge. It would later form a new union with an Apostate Champion who also greatly hated Amiable Community Custodian, forming a new, nightmarish enemy for the hero.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T08:10:04-08:00","id":1286713,"title":"","content":"Did anyone else have a take on Venom that they wanted to share?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T09:31:24-08:00","id":1286752,"title":"","content":"Who Sits on the Webbed Throne<br /> <br /> This Yozi is the patron of all those who exert power through domination of the context of situations. Like the general Belisarius, it calculates angles, not figures. Unlike many Yozi, however, it embraces its ability to change its nature through changing its Fetich soul (if that is indeed still a thing in 3E). Because of its portfolio, changing the Fetich soul cannot change its intrinsic nature to a contradiction of its name.<br /> <br /> As such, it can appear as a webslinging friendly neighborhood hero, an enigmatic masked private detective, a kid who can turn invisible, or even a Warstrider to be piloted by a trusted boon companion, if any could so exist.<br /> <br /> The danger WSotWT presents is that if it changes soul too well, Creation can fracture or even bifurcate so that both souls and therefore Creations are true, creating existential issues for the Pattern Spiders, who were WSotWT's original servants who rebelled after WSotWT's machinations caused them to be irradiated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3551-ulthwithian","name":"Ulthwithian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T11:13:27-07:00","id":1298993,"title":"","content":"New York is a city being transformed into a Satrapy by the Realm through economic pressure and espionage rather than military force. So far, the elder Dragonblood known as the King Pin has managed to hide his role as the mastermind behind this take over while posing as a virtuous figure to the local populace.<br /> <br /> A local Lunar Exalt known as the Man-Spider refused to join the Silver Pact because he wanted to focus solely upon fighting the King Pin to free his home, despite his elders regarding the matter as a lost cause. While the Man-Spider has consistently failed to expose the King Pin as an enemy to his people, he has successfully thwarted many of schemes that would have led to the total surrender of the city to Dynastic control.<br /> <br /> Miles Morales is Chosen by Luna in a battle that ends with the King Pin finally killing the Man-Spider, just after the older Lunar had promised to teach him everything he knew.<br /> <br /> Miles is left Casteless, alone, and terrified until the Silver Pact arrives.<br /> <br /> Leading the team is Peter B. Parker, a Lunar even older than the Man-Spider, who came only out of begrudging obligation. It turns out that he's actually been rather envious of the Man-Spider's glorious career despite its shorter length.<br /> <br /> The older Lunars help Miles adjust to his new role in the world and decide for himself what kind of Lunar he wants to be. Ultimately, he decides to stay and continue the Man-Spider's war against the King Pin after the other Lunars grant him his tattoos and leave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}